  "summary": "Recent preprints and a 2026 study test how visual feedback, practice and mechanical loading modulate muscle activation and afferent signaling.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is how muscle activity is reorganized by sensory information, practice and external mechanical loading. In 14 healthy adults, real-time augmented-reality biofeedback of quadriceps HDsEMG activity shifted activation laterally and increased endurance during dynamic knee extensions. In older adults, split-belt walking practice produced smaller reductions in reactive muscle activity than in younger adults, whereas context-specific muscle patterns were retained. In anesthetized rats, parallel exoskeleton-like springs altered muscle fascicle dynamics and force without changing primary muscle spindle firing, suggesting that mechanical modulation of the muscle-tendon unit can dissociate from afferent output. The items differ in species and paradigm, so the shared theme is methodological: spatially resolved, context-dependent readouts of muscle activation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
